openViewDesigner: use per-view draft or saved definition; show selected control properties, indented layout and live preview.
renderViewControlProperties: offer type-specific labels, text, getter/setter/action selectors, typed arguments, slider bounds and table columns.
addViewControl: insert within selected container or after a selected leaf; wrap a leaf root as needed.
changeViewControl: move among siblings, nest into preceding container, lift after parent, duplicate subtree or remove; protect root.
previewViewDesigner: use ordinary renderer with path decoration; highlight selection, intercept click/Enter/Space before action/setter handlers, and read live getters.
toggleViewDesignerJSON: validate and switch representations while preserving extra fields and invalid raw drafts.
saveViewDesigner: validate and send definition: to InspectorView; refresh live receiver and preview.
reloadViewDesigner: read stored definition and discard both visual and raw drafts.
closeViewDesigner: remember drafts by view object and dismiss.

Show live control identity, inspector link, inherited/explicit receiver and Wiring action selection. Read authoritative definition after save, retain control IDs on edits/moves, strip IDs on duplicate, and preserve only unsaved drafts.
